  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: ⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive). Pattern: X⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{撫|な}でる (to stroke X).\n\nASPECT: ている indicates ongoing action. {撫|な}でている = 'is stroking.'\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ⟦{頭|あたま}→頭：00574_atama⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{撫|な}でる (to pat on the head)\n- ⟦{背中|せなか}→背中：00810_senaka⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{撫|な}でる (to stroke one's back)\n- ⟦{髪|かみ}→髪：02196_kami⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{撫|な}でる (to stroke hair)\n- {撫|な}で⟦{下|お}ろす→下ろす：02029_orosu⟧ (to stroke downward - also: to feel relieved)\n\nIDIOM: ⟦{胸|むね}→胸：00972_mune⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{撫|な}で⟦{下|お}ろす→下ろす：02029_orosu⟧ - to feel relieved (lit. 'stroke down one's chest').\n\nCULTURAL NOTE: Stroking a child's head is a common sign of affection in Japan. The expression ⟦{頭|あたま}→頭：00574_atama⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{撫|な}でる often appears in positive contexts.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦{触|さわ}る→触る：00808_sawaru⟧ - to touch (neutral)\n- ⟦{叩|たた}く→叩く：02072_tataku⟧ - to tap, pat (with more force)",
